From bdc4a839eeb2b61fb7558ca4b8b1ff17014ca6d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:01:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] Try-on browser libraries: photo prep, session, client,
 copy and one-tap line

The phone side of the try-on, with no screens yet. Photo prep decodes upright
(EXIF 1, 3, 6 and 8 proven in Chromium on both decode paths), cuts the 3:4
frame and writes a fresh 1152x1536 JPEG with no EXIF or GPS: 168 ms at 1x and
727 ms median at 4x CPU for a 4000x3000 photo. The tab session keeps one photo
per kind and each preview by piece and stone, and revokes every blob URL on
Delete, pagehide and 30 minutes idle. The XHR client sends only meta and photo
and maps every server code to the spec's words. Also: device id (never
naira_vid), sceneGuard in log mode, an allow-listed Clarity wrapper, the copy
deck, share and save, and oneTapLine for the Add button. 143 tests (617).

src/data/tryOnHandles.ts is a placeholder for the manifest engineer's file.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TpEhS3XnffjKP5JTdNrd3V
